00:07:44.064 --> 00:07:46.731
"If you flunk, you'll be bagger.

00:07:47.808 --> 00:07:50.407
"You better study, go college."

00:07:50.407 --> 00:07:53.574
So, I really appreciated that teacher.

00:07:54.574 --> 00:07:56.901
He's like my father.

00:07:56.901 --> 00:07:59.068
He guide me what I am now.

00:08:00.424 --> 00:08:01.257
So...

00:08:03.917 --> 00:08:07.608
For me, even I didn't have a father,

00:08:07.608 --> 00:08:10.292
I would rather need a father figure,

00:08:10.292 --> 00:08:12.375
somebody who can discuss.

00:08:14.249 --> 00:08:16.102
- 'Cause I know that there
were, I didn't mean it,

00:08:16.102 --> 00:08:18.325
but there were times that I
screamed that I hated you.

00:08:18.325 --> 00:08:19.219
There were times that I told you

00:08:19.219 --> 00:08:21.377
to fuck off and leave my room.

00:08:21.377 --> 00:08:22.757
- Yes.

00:08:22.757 --> 00:08:24.380
I know you did that, but
you didn't really mean it,

00:08:24.380 --> 00:08:25.760
you were just angry.

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:26.760
- But how's,

00:08:29.110 --> 00:08:31.393
I don't know, how's that feel as a dad?

00:08:31.393 --> 00:08:34.109
- Well, I'm smarter and
more mature than that,

00:08:34.109 --> 00:08:35.028
so when you said that,

00:08:35.028 --> 00:08:38.322
I knew to take it with a grain of salt.

00:08:38.322 --> 00:08:40.084
- I guess I've, I've
never apologized for it

00:08:40.084 --> 00:08:42.667
and I've felt bad about it, so.

00:08:43.612 --> 00:08:45.095
I wanted to say I'm sorry.

00:08:45.095 --> 00:08:45.928
- I just don't understand why you don't

00:08:45.928 --> 00:08:49.012
say any of this when we were growing up.

00:08:49.012 --> 00:08:51.762
- Well, I guess, it's my mistake.

00:08:52.784 --> 00:08:54.130
Now we can talk.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.399
- Yeah.

00:08:55.399 --> 00:08:56.531
Were you just not comfortable?

00:08:56.531 --> 00:08:57.864
- Right.

00:08:57.864 --> 00:08:59.562
- Do you think it's
because, Korean culture?

00:08:59.562 --> 00:09:03.883
- Well, because I didn't know
my father and my mother left,

00:09:03.883 --> 00:09:07.689
so then I'm not very
proud to talk about it.

00:09:07.689 --> 00:09:09.272
- Yeah, but I just feel like,

00:09:09.272 --> 00:09:10.432
you didn't have to go through that

00:09:10.432 --> 00:09:12.184
by yourself all the time.

00:09:12.184 --> 00:09:14.351
- Well, I wasted all that.

00:09:17.346 --> 00:09:20.545
Make a strong person, but other side,

00:09:20.545 --> 00:09:22.281
make you very weak.

00:09:22.281 --> 00:09:25.342
- I don't know if I've
really told you this yet,

00:09:25.342 --> 00:09:28.509
but Arielle and I are actually, kinda,

00:09:29.629 --> 00:09:32.112
trying to start having kids this year.

00:09:32.112 --> 00:09:32.945
- Wow.

00:09:32.945 --> 00:09:35.712
What do you think about that?

00:09:35.712 --> 00:09:37.584
- I feel like it's something that we've

00:09:37.584 --> 00:09:39.954
been talking about for a while, and--

00:09:39.954 --> 00:09:43.653
- Yeah, I've noticed the
pregnancy books in the,

00:09:43.653 --> 00:09:44.943
